# Seventh-Chord Arpeggios in C (repertoire plan: st-arpeggio-sevenths). An original study in fifth
# position (the G-shape position of C major: finger 1 on fret 5, finger 4 on fret 8; B on string 3
# fret 4 is finger 1 reaching back one fret), eighth notes, alternate picking.
# Bars 1-7: the seven seventh chords of C major, one bar each, each from its root up to the octave
# and back down to the third (root, 3, 5, 7, octave, 7, 5, 3); the next bar starts one step lower
# than that third, on the next root:
#   Cmaj7 C E G B   Dm7 D F A C   Em7 E G B D   Fmaj7 F A C E   G7 G B D F   Am7 A C E G   Bm7b5 B D F A
# Bar 8: Cmaj7 again an octave higher, landing on the high C.
# Bars 9-16: an 8-bar tune over Dm7 | G7 | Cmaj7 | Cmaj7, twice, built from the same chord tones.
# Strong beats are chord tones; the guide tones move F (Dm7, G7) to E (Cmaj7) and C to B.
# Every note is in the engine's G-shape pattern of C major, with its finger.
# The teacher strums each chord in its open-position shape.
title: Seventh-Chord Arpeggios in C
